      "description": "Overshot crimp cloth. The complete540-end threading joins the four printed lines and expands the3× repeat. This draft represents a ruffled end border. Weave½ inch plain-weave hems and a71-inch plain-weave body with an upholstery gathering pick after each6 ground picks. Gather, steam-set40 minutes, dry, then remove the gathering threads; finishing creates the crimped body.",
